    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d607-a8">

                <pb facs="0682" n="602" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg602"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 8.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Commander Nickels to Mr. Powell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">U.
                                S. S. Topeka</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                            Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-05-29"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 29,
                    1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Vice-Admiral Killick, flying his flag on
                    the cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Crête à Pierrot</hi>, arrived and anchored
                    in the port this afternoon. I sent an officer on board to find out whether the
                    Admiral was under the orders of the Provisional Government, and was informed
                    that he was.</p>
                <p>I have requested him to dress ship and fire a national salute to-morrow in honor
                    of our holiday, which he will do. I shall salute his flag to-morrow morning, and
                    call upon him later in the day</p>
                <p>Yours, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John A. H. Nickels</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Commander, U. S. Navy.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
